 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
+## Threshold Support
+- The `--threshold <metric>=<min>` CLI option allows gating CI pipelines on metric scores.
+- Multiple thresholds can be specified by repeating the option: `--threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95`.
+- Thresholds must be valid metric IDs (exact_match, toxicity, length_variance, or custom metric ids) with scores between 0 and 1.
+- If any threshold fails (metric score < min or metric has no score), `frai eval` exits with code 1; otherwise exits 0.
+- Malformed thresholds (invalid format or out-of-range values) exit with code 2.
+- SDK users pass thresholds via `generateReport({ evaluations, thresholds: { exact_match: 0.9 } })`.
+- Reports record threshold outcomes: JSON reports gain `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array of results); Markdown reports show a "Thresholds" section with PASS/FAIL status for each.
+
 ## Follow-up Tasks
 1. Integrate real toxicity/bias models once provider abstraction is implemented (Phase 0 → Providers milestone).
 2. Extend datasets loader to support configurable schema mapping.
